      "rationale": "A second implementation of the `s.block.block2d` node-kind document and all twenty-six typed mutations, in Python, at `../../../../../🧪️tests/mutate-block-2d-1/🐍️component.py`. Written from `../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/🔣️.json` (the ten members), `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/🔣️.json` and `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio` (the twenty-six verbs and their argument lists), and the twenty-six committed `(before, mutation, after, outcome)` specification vectors — which give the internally tagged wire form of each verb and the two things only they state: that `update-presentation` REBUILDS the presentation from its six arguments and drops every member whose argument is null, and that an `author` keeps only the members it was given. It imports nothing from this repository and transliterates none of its Rust. A third-party library was declined, not merely absent: a symbol- or component-library format such as KiCad, Modelica or IFC's property sets carries pins or ports but has no notion of a kind-level compatibility relation between handle kinds, of a rim angle in radians, or of the presentation variant this vocabulary switches with one verb, and none of them reads this carrier. `package` is deliberately empty: the implementation needs no distribution, so this entry contributes nothing to `🔒️dependencies.json`.\n\nUNDER PROTOCOL V2 this registration is classified `cross-semio-implementation` — a required SUPPLEMENTAL oracle that does not discharge `block-2d-1-mutate`'s external-oracle requirement for its 26-kind mutation vocabulary; a qualifying third-party reference (`third-party-library` / `third-party-cli` / `standards-reference-tool`) is still owed.\n\n[2026-09-02, D1 — SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION] Promoted from cross-semio-implementation to verified-native-second-implementation: this artifact is semio-native (isSemioNativeArtifact), this reference's own third-party survey above (kept verbatim) already names what was checked and declined, its python implementation differs from the Rust subject, and it covers 100% of this manifest's 1 capability/capabilities with 26 committed fixture vector(s). See .🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️09/☀️02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION/📓️d1-native-oracle-discharge.md.",
